---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import TerminalPrompt from '../components/TerminalPrompt.astro';
import AsciiBox from '../components/AsciiBox.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`risu-mcp privacy policy — ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="Privacy policy for risu-mcp, a private tool that reads my own Google Analytics and Search Console data." noindex />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<TerminalPrompt command="cat PRIVACY" />

			<AsciiBox title="risu-mcp privacy policy" heading="h1">
				<p class="updated">Last updated: 29 September 2026</p>

				<h2>What it is</h2>
				<p>
					risu-mcp is a private tool, and I (Andrzej Białaś, risu) am its only user. It connects my own
					Google account to the AI assistant I work with on my computer. It runs only there, and it isn't
					offered to anyone else.
				</p>

				<h2>What it can access</h2>
				<p>
					When I sign in, Google gives it access to Google Analytics and Google Search Console for the
					websites I run, such as risu.pl and skillcraft.cloud. It reads traffic and search reports, and it
					can submit sitemaps and indexing requests for those sites. I use that access for nothing else.
				</p>

				<h2>How the data is used</h2>
				<p>
					Reports are fetched to my computer when I ask for them. My AI assistant (Claude Code, made by
					Anthropic) reads them to help me understand how my sites are doing. That's the only use.
				</p>

				<h2>Where it's kept</h2>
				<p>
					The sign-in tokens stay on my computer. Reports I build from the data stay in my private files.
				</p>

				<h2>What it never does</h2>
				<p>
					It doesn't sell the data, use it for advertising, or pass it to anyone beyond that assistant. It
					never touches anyone else's Google account.
				</p>

				<h2>Removing access</h2>
				<p>
					Access can be revoked at any time at
					<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
				</p>

				<h2>Contact</h2>
				<p>
					My contact links are on <a href="/me">my about page</a>.
				</p>
			</AsciiBox>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.updated {
		margin: 0 0 1.25em;
		color: var(--text-muted);
		font-size: 0.85em;
	}
	h2 {
		margin: 1.4em 0 0.4em;
		font-size: 1em;
		color: var(--text-bright);
	}
	p {
		margin: 0 0 0.8em;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}
	a {
		color: var(--cyan);
	}
</style>
